<mxCell id="g_c1" value="" style="pointerEvents=1;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;shadow=0;dashed=0;align=center;html=1;verticalAlign=top;shape=mxgraph.electrical.signal_sources.signal_ground;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#000000;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1568" y="600" width="24" height="16" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e42" value="" style="html=1;rounded=0;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#212121;jumpStyle=arc;jumpSize=8;endArrow=none;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c1" target="g_c1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
<mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;NOTES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. ⏚ = GND. Every ground symbol is the same node: PSU −, buck IN−/OUT−, Nano GND, HC-SR04 GND, Q1 emitter, both strips.&lt;br&gt;2. U1: adjust to 5.0V with a multimeter &lt;i&gt;before&lt;/i&gt; connecting the load. 5V feeds the Nano 5V pin directly (not VIN).&lt;br&gt;3. D7 HIGH → Q1 saturates → coil current +12V → K1 coil → Q1 C→E → GND → K1 switches COM to NO → LED1 ON.&lt;br&gt;4. D1 across the coil, cathode (stripe) to +12V. If it's reversed, D1 shorts +12V through Q1 when it turns on.&lt;br&gt;5. Q1 C1815 TO-92 pinout: flat face toward you, legs down → E · C · B. Verify against the datasheet.&lt;br&gt;6. K1 pins differ between brands. Identify them with a multimeter: coil ≈ 100–1000Ω, COM–NC = 0Ω at rest.&lt;br&gt;7. R2 and C1 go as close to LED2 as possible. Limit WS2812 brightness in firmware (≈60 mA/LED at full white).&lt;br&gt;8. F1 / COM / NO / LED1 wiring carries the full strip current: use thicker wire there." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;spacing=10;strokeColor=#BDBDBD;fillColor=#FAFAFA;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="900" width="1160" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;WIRES&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;font color='#C62828'&gt;━ +12V&lt;/font&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color='#7F0000'&gt;━ switched +12V&lt;/font&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color='#E65100'&gt;━ +5V&lt;/font&gt; &amp;nbsp; ━ GND &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color='#1565C0'&gt;━ data&lt;/font&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color='#2E7D32'&gt;━ relay control&lt;/font&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color='#6A1B9A'&gt;━ coil low side&lt;/font&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;font color='#757575'&gt;┅ mechanical&lt;/font&gt; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; ● junction &amp;nbsp; ⌒ crossing, no connection" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;spacing=10;strokeColor=#BDBDBD;fillColor=#FAFAFA;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1100" width="1160" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="titleblock" value="&lt;table style='width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px;' border='1' cellpadding='6'&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan='2' style='font-size:16px;'&gt;&lt;b&gt;BigPP gen3 – Wiring Diagram&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style='width:35%;'&gt;Project&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Ultrasonic-triggered LED controller&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Controller&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Arduino Nano (ATmega328P)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Supply&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;12V DC → 5V buck&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Author&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Lorenzo Venerandi&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Date&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;2026-10-22&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Rev&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;B&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;strokeColor=#424242;fillColor=#FFFFFF;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1240" y="900" width="480" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
